r parenteral nutrition.", "COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS:\"COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS\" refers to infectious complications that can arise in surgical patients, particularly in those with cancer. These complications are significant adverse effects that may occur post-surgery and are often addressed in the context of nutritional support. One specific risk associated with these complications is lipoid pneumonia due to aspiration, which can be linked to the ketogenic diet. To mitigate the health issues that may arise after surgery, the use of immunomodulatory formulas is recommended. Overall, \"COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS\" encompasses a range of infectious risks that necessitate careful management and nutritional strategies to improve patient outcomes.", "PEDRO JOSÉ PINÉS CORRALES:Pedro José Pinés Corrales is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the University Hospital Complex of Albacete and an associate professor at the Faculty of Medicine of Albacete, University of Castilla-La Mancha.", "UNIVERSIDAD DE CASTILLA-LA MANCHA:The University of Castilla-La Mancha is an educational institution where Pedro José Pinés Corrales serves as an associate professor in Endocrinology and Nutrition.", "ACADÉMIA CTO-MEDICINA:The CTO-Medicine Academy is an educational institution where Pedro José Pinés Corrales teaches Endocrinology, Metabolism, and Nutrition.", "ADRENOLEUCODISTROFIA:Adrenoleucodistrofia, also known as adrenoleukodystrophy, is a hereditary genetic disorder that affects lipid metabolism, specifically the metabolism of very long-chain fatty acids. This condition is characterized by the abnormal accumulation of these fatty acids in the body, which primarily impacts the myelin sheath of the nervous system and the adrenal cortex. As a result, individuals with adrenoleucodistrofia experience a range of neurological decline and various metabolic issues, including problems related to the adrenal glands.\n\nThe disorder is notable for its variable phenotypic expression, meaning that symptoms can differ significantly among affected individuals. It is relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases due to its overlapping symptoms. Management of adrenoleucodistrofia often requires dietary interventions to help mitigate the effects of the disorder. Overall, adrenoleucodistrofia represents a complex interplay of genetic and metabolic factors that necessitate careful clinical attention.", "CYP21A2:CYP21A2 is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the production of 21-hydroxylase, and its deficiency can lead to primary adrenal insufficiency. This condition is particularly significant in young males who exhibit symptoms of adrenal insufficiency. The diagnosis of adrenal insufficiency often involves the detection of antibodies related to CYP21A2, highlighting its importance in clinical assessments. Additionally, the gene CYP21A2 is responsible for encoding the enzyme, and its deficiency is a known cause of congenital adrenal hyperplasia.", "HOSPITAL COMPLEJO UNIVERSITARIO DE ALBACETE:The Hospital Complex of Albacete is a healthcare facility where various medical specialties, including Endocrinology, are practiced.", "ANEMIA PERNICIOSA:Anemia perniciosa is an autoimmune condition characterized by impaired absorption of vitamin B12. This disorder can be associated with various other autoimmune diseases, including autoimmune thyroid diseases and type 1 diabetes mellitus. Additionally, it is frequently linked to primary adrenal insufficiency.", "GEN X-ALD:The GEN X-ALD gene is responsible for encoding a protein that functions as a peroxisomal membrane transporter, specifically involved in the transport of fatty acids within cells. Mutations in the X-ALD gene result in a condition known as adrenoleukodystrophy, which is characterized by the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids due to impaired transport. This genetic alteration can lead to severe neurological and adrenal dysfunction, highlighting the critical role of the X-ALD gene in cellular fatty acid metabolism.", "SÍNDROME PLURIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 2:El síndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2 es una condición genética que se caracteriza por la presencia de múltiples enfermedades autoinmunitarias, incluyendo insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria.", "HLA-DR3:HLA-DR3 is a genetic region that is associated with type 2 autoimmune polyglandular syndrome, as well as other autoimmune diseases. It is classified as a histocompatibility antigen, playing a significant role in the immune system's response.", "DIABETES TIPO 1:Diabetes tipo 1 es una enfermedad crónica que afecta la forma en que el cuerpo metaboliza la glucosa, resultando en niveles elevados de glucosa en sangre. Esta condición es una enfermedad autoinmunitaria, en la cual el sistema inmunológico ataca las células productoras de insulina en el páncreas, lo que lleva a la incapacidad del cuerpo para producir insulina. Como resultado, los pacientes con diabetes tipo 1 requieren un manejo y tratamiento de por vida para controlar sus niveles de glucosa en sangre.\n\nAdemás, la diabetes tipo 1 es un área principal de investigación para Martín Cuesta Hernández, quien se enfoca en su tratamiento y gestión. También se ha observado que la diabetes tipo 1 puede tener una mayor prevalencia entre pacientes con trastornos alimentarios, como la Anorexia Nerviosa. Aunque menos frecuentemente, esta enfermedad puede estar asociada con el síndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2.", "FALLO OVÁRICO PRECOZ:El fallo ovárico precoz es una condición que puede estar asociada con el síndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2, afectando la función reproductiva en mujeres jóvenes.", "HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA:\"Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna\" is a comprehensive medical textbook edited by a team of experts including Kasper DL, Hauser SL, Jameson JL, Fauci AS, Longo DL, and Loscazo J. This authoritative reference provides extensive information on various aspects of internal medicine, covering a wide range of medical conditions and treatments. Notably, it includes detailed discussions on adrenal disorders, such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia and pheochromocytoma, as well as other endocrine disorders. The textbook is widely recognized and utilized in the medical field for its thorough guidelines and insights into internal medicine, making it an essential resource for healthcare professionals."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}